# Local scratch material and local-history notes — deliberately kept out of the
# published tarball.
#
# Why this file lives in docs/ instead of the package root: a root .npmignore
# does NOT override package.json's "files" field, but one in a subdirectory does.
# Without it, `files: ["docs"]` would publish these files (npm pack reads the
# working tree, so .gitignore alone does not keep them out).
#
# The user's own working notes.
desktop-panel-kickoff-prompt.md
desktop-panel-prompt-short.md
optimization-plan.md

# Local-history documents: they record THIS machine — the ssh alias, the server
# address, local paths, backup directories. They stay in the git repository
# (where they are the project's own history) but never travel to npm.
desktop-panel-progress.md
desktop-panel-0.2.1-plan.md
desktop-web-refactor-route.md
